    "overview": "AI Image Detector.info is an image authenticity verification tool that analyzes images to determine whether they are AI-generated or real. It uses four independent AI detection models and combines their results through a published weighted-vote system, while showing the evidence from each detection engine rather than hiding it behind a single confidence score. The platform reports disagreements between detection models instead of suppressing conflicting results and can analyze up to 50 images at once for bulk screening. It also checks C2PA credentials and generator self-tags, which can provide additional evidence and may override model results when the provenance information is definitive. Use Cases AI Image Detection: Determine whether an image was generated or modified using AI. Image Authenticity: Verify whether digital images appear authentic or AI-generated. Bulk Image Screening: Analyze up to 50 images simultaneously for faster verification. Profile Photo Verification: Screen profile and dating photos for potential AI generation. Marketplace Safety: Help online marketplaces identify suspicious AI-generated product images. Product Image Verification: Check ecommerce product and listing photos for signs of AI generation. Digital Art Analysis: Verify the origin and authenticity of digital artwork. News Verification: Screen images used in news stories and editorial research. Viral Image Checking: Investigate potentially AI-generated images circulating online. Social Media Verification: Analyze reposted images before sharing or publishing them. C2PA Verification: Check available C2PA credentials and provenance information. Generator Tag Detection: Identify self-declared generator tags that can provide additional evidence about an image's origin. Forensic Screening: Compare multiple independent detection signals when investigating image authenticity. Transparent Detection: Review individual model results and identify disagreements instead of relying on one hidden score. Content Moderation: Support platforms and communities in screening potentially synthetic visual content.",
